    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but is it really a rebellion? it feels more like just delaying the inevitable. if the destination doesn't exist, then the movement is just pointless motion. it's hard to find the \"rebellion\" in just suffering through something that has no end and no goal. sometimes i feel like the most logical thing to do is just stop the motion altogether. it's like, if the play is bad and there's no point to the story, why stay until the lights go out?",
